id: pm-gh1485
title: "GH-1485: Bound history-index reader contention before authoritative appends"
description: "Evaluate and bound writer delay from exclusive history-event-index readers while preserving authoritative history, invalidation, fallback and late-fact visibility. The reported mixed reader/writer workload retained correctness but breached its 2000ms real-time delivery SLO in one traced run."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[4]: "area:history","area:locking",github-intake,performance
created_at: "2026-10-16T13:01:36.615Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-17T23:06:09.623Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-17T23:06:08.693Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-17T23:06:08.693Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 240
acceptance_criteria: "Reproduce with isolated traced and untraced cohorts and report writer lock wait separately from downstream detection; Choose and document a bounded snapshot/fair-lock/critical-section protocol from measured attribution; Preserve authoritative fallback, committed invalidation and late-fact visibility; Prove zero lost or duplicate events, zero history drift and the declared end-to-end latency budget under mixed SDK and CLI writers."
goal: project management = context management
objective: Measure reader-versus-writer lock attribution and implement a bounded history-index read/write protocol without losing committed facts.
value: UI and agent watchers can observe project context without delaying authoritative mutations beyond a measured collaboration budget.
why_now: GH-1485 reports a 2247.5ms pre-append delay with at least 2071.0ms waiting for the history-index lock under 100 readers and ten writer lanes.
parent: pm-lvyd
risk: high
confidence: medium
severity: medium
resolution: "Capture SQLite rows and size receipts coherently, close before asynchronous validation, and observe token-owned append progress. Preserve native contention markers until zero-wait recovery probes clear; authoritative writers bypass the projection lock through portable invalidation, while repair rejects changed snapshots and yields during construction."
expected_result: Keep complete authoritative history while avoiding projection-induced writer queues and meeting the fixed-boundary mixed-reader budget without changing cursor contracts or quality thresholds.
actual_result: "Complete final pnpm quality:static and all four typecheck projects pass. Linked history/workflow70 tests and focused history/SDK/lock/workflow388 tests pass; deterministic controls cover paused append, paused repair, returning native contention, settled damage and expired leases. Traced/untraced100-reader cohorts each deliver5000 unique observations with zero drift and maxima1154/1212ms below2000ms. Required observability gate passes; current-version backend243 starts/243 finishes with max2412ms ingestion. Full final-head hosted coverage/analyzer admission is required before merge; timestamp-cursor ordering remains separately tracked."
component: history event index concurrency
